keywords:
  - InSAR
  - Sentinel-1
  - Ridgecrest earthquake
  - crustal strain
  - strain tensor
  - change detection
  - GNSS
  - Gaussian process
  - cokriging
  - earthquake geodesy

abstract: >-
  Reproducible software for deriving cumulative two-dimensional horizontal strain from
  dual-track Sentinel-1 InSAR displacement time series. The workflow removes a
  GNSS-constrained vertical field from each line of sight with full uncertainty
  propagation, inverts the corrected horizontal pair for cumulative east-north
  displacement, estimates the full 2-D strain tensor on a fixed local affine operator,
  reconstructs near-fault gaps with fault-barrier-aware cokriging, and tests temporal
  change using calibrated strain innovations with family-wise error control. Applied to
  80 epochs spanning May 2017 to November 2019 over the 2019 Ridgecrest earthquake
  sequence.

